cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use uibc-core or UIBC in academic work, please cite the entry below.
  SCOPE, stated because it is easy to get wrong: this entry pins the 0.5.5
  archive (2026-11-26), whose verifier implements the same checks as the
  repository -- S1-S19, plus S0 as a fallback branch. The doi field points at
  the CONCEPT DOI on purpose: it always resolves to the latest release, so it
  cannot go stale the way a version DOI does. Two earlier versions remain
  valid for their own snapshots and must not be attributed more than they
  carry: 0.2.1 (10.5281/zenodo.22821835) holds only six checks, S1-S6, and
  0.4.2 (10.5281/zenodo.24375013) predates the 40-repository parity table, so
  neither may be cited for material added in 0.5.5. docs/ARCHIVE-GAP.md
  records the 0.2.1 measurement and how the gap was closed, and
  tools/check_citation_scope.py recomputes it from the baseline files in
  docs/.
type: software
title: "uibc-core: Verifiable Evidence Packages for Autonomous AI Agents"
abstract: >-
  uibc-core is a reference implementation of UIBC (Uniform Identity-Behavior Chain):
  verifiable evidence packages for autonomous AI agents, built on the LGD principles
  of Registry, Evidence and Gates. Every agent action can be sealed into a
  submission.uibc package (identity + lifecycle events + content-hashed evidence +
  evidence root + optional seal), then verified offline.
  Scope of this archived version: S1-S19 (S0 is a fallback branch, not a
  separate check); the bundled 28-case corpus exercises 15 of the 20 ids, and
  says so in its own README.
